# Next.js / App Router

This is **Next.js 16**, not classic Next 13/14 training data. Before new APIs or file conventions, check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` and heed deprecations (`AGENTS.md`).

## Conventions in this repo

- App code lives under `src/app` (not root `app/`).
- Route groups: `(auth)` for unauthenticated pages, `(app)` for the driver shell.
- Middleware: `src/middleware.ts` → `updateSession` from `@/lib/supabase/middleware`. Keep Serwist/static paths excluded in `matcher`.
- `reactCompiler: true` in `next.config.ts` — avoid unnecessary `useMemo`/`useCallback` unless profiling shows need.
- Prefer Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only for camera, geo, canvas, interactive forms, or browser Supabase auth UI.
- Route handlers return `NextResponse.json(...)`; stubs may use `501` until wired.

## PWA touchpoints

- SW entry: `src/app/sw.ts`; provider wraps root layout via `@/components/pwa/serwist-provider`.
- Offline fallback page: `src/app/~offline/page.tsx`.
- Do not break Serwist routes (`/serwist/*`) or the middleware exclusion list.

## Env

Document new vars in `.env.local.example` only (names, no secrets). Public: `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`. Server-only: `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `R2_*`, `DATABASE_URL` / `DIRECT_URL`.
